ABSTRACT

This report presents the design and implementation of a full-stack, multi-server, AI-enabled Student Academic Assistant system tailored for NIT Jalandhar. The system addresses a practical and common problem in educational institutions: delivering accurate, secure, and context-aware responses for both student-specific and institution-level academic queries.

Unlike a traditional single-layer chatbot, the project adopts a three-server architecture in which each server has a dedicated responsibility. The first layer is a React/Next.js frontend dashboard that handles login, chat interaction, voice-enabled read-aloud, and real-time response rendering through Server-Sent Events. The second layer is a Python FastAPI orchestration backend that performs authentication, validates tokens, manages the conversational workflow through LangGraph, routes requests to domain-specific nodes, and coordinates tool calls and RAG retrieval. The third layer is a Spring Boot server configured as an MCP (Model Context Protocol) tool provider that exposes strongly typed academic and profile tools backed by JPA repositories and MySQL.

The project combines two complementary intelligence modes. For unstructured policy and curriculum information, a RAG pipeline is implemented using PDF ingestion, chunking, Gemini embeddings, and FAISS retrieval. For structured student and admin analytics, Spring MCP tools query relational tables such as students, attendance, academic_performance, subjects, internships, and placements. This hybrid approach ensures factual grounding, reduced hallucination, and useful personalized responses.

Security has been treated as a first-class requirement. Student passwords are verified against Argon2 hashes, JWT tokens are issued with role claims and expiry, and admin operations are guarded by explicit role checks in orchestration logic. Operational stability considerations include timeout boundaries for MCP calls and graceful fallback responses in case of LLM quota exhaustion.

The resulting platform demonstrates a practical blueprint for educational AI systems that need to integrate conversational UX, secure role-aware access, deterministic tool execution, and document-grounded question answering. This report documents complete architecture, modules, schemas, sequence flows, implementation decisions, trade-offs, and future enhancement directions.


